<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58619" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολλόροβον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shepherd's staff</i> or
			<i>crook</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				759.13
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">ii A.D.</span>, written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολλωρ</span>-); applied to the so-called <i>club</i> of <i><span class="en">
				Orion
			</span></i> and Bootes (which has this form), <i><span class="en">
				Hipparch.
				1.7.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.6.1b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Alm.</u>
				7.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> masc. and
			neut., dub. sens., apptly. a weight or a coin, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				6954
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> pl., 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιλλοβόροι</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.143
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολόροβοι</span>, 
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοιά</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολόροβον</span>, 
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κορύνη</span>
			, Id.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
